+# 08 — VS CSS: gate-opening stalls and flashing
+
+**Version:** runtime-candidate research revision, 2026-09-14.
+**Inspected base:** `a5c5bc08d8e8661658865216798d600462db948e` (`master`).
+**Priority / scope:** Flashing/corruption first; then frame pacing.
+**Existing owner:** P2-1 CSS presentation.
+**Status:** OPEN — candidate code/proposals, not a ROM-verified fix.
+
+Read [COMMON.md](COMMON.md). Reconcile the actual working tree, source-derived
+assets and current board before changing code. Preserve unrelated edits.
+
+## Owner report (preserved)
+
+> Low FPS/Flashing during gate openings
+
+## Current source findings
+
+The compact-preview action budget is already present. The acquisition still performs blocking work inside that action, so one action per tick does not bound its time. R03 closes reset-order gaps but not gate animation cost.
+
+Source keys: [S10](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#s10), [R48](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r48), [R102](research/SOURCE_LEDGER.md#r102).
+These distinguish directly inspected code from repository-recorded proof; none
+is a new ROM run by this package's author.
+
+## Potential runtime fix
+
+Implement the bounded preview transaction in research/CSS_TRANSACTIONAL_PREVIEW.md. Split payload, relocation, native image load and pose preparation into budgeted phases; publish one complete preview identity only at a safe presentation boundary. Keep the gate animation and already-visible preview drawing while an acquisition is pending. Cache unchanged menu surfaces/matrices and avoid repeated texture uploads after residency. Attribute flashing independently: inspect BG/OBJ/GX bank ownership, generation retirement and publish order; repair the first premature visibility or stale binding rather than hiding gates or reducing simulation arbitrarily.
+
+### Executable candidate diffs
+
+[R03_css_reset_image_lifetime.patch](runtime/R03_css_reset_image_lifetime.patch) — **DEFENSIVE CANDIDATE / not a complete CSS fix**.
+
+Check preimages with `python Briefs/tools/check_candidates.py --repo . --candidate R03`. Applying a patch and passing a host test do not establish natural-path correctness.
+
+Implementation contract and code-oriented integration details: [research/CSS_TRANSACTIONAL_PREVIEW.md](research/CSS_TRANSACTIONAL_PREVIEW.md).
+
+## Disprove this candidate before stacking patches
+
+If a gate-only resident run still hitches without acquisition, the bottleneck is not the loader. Profile the gate draw and display-bank commit separately. Do not add another action-budget decrement.
+
+## Acceptance for this symptom
+
+Entire gate-open/close cycles render without flashes, garbage, missed source states or input stalls. Record all-presented-frame 2/3/4/5+ VBlank histogram, max interval and P50/P95 against a matching baseline. Meet the current menu cadence target; a faster average that retains conspicuous flashes fails.
+
+## Required regression scope
+
+Preview residency, all menu surfaces, gate timing and source behavior, BGM/announcer audio, repeat entry and four-panel memory limits.
+
+## Coordination
+
+Coordinate with preview latency and music briefs; one shared repair may satisfy several distinct captures.
+
+## Closure
+
+Apply COMMON.md's natural-path, positive-engagement, source/pixel/audio, resource,
+native-only, cadence and widest-relevant-verifier requirements. Record candidate
+identity and actual coverage in the existing BUG_NOTES owner; preserve BUGS wording
+and unrelated dirty edits. Report any unrun/failed gate and owner acceptance still
+owed. No brief or host-only test closes the runtime bug. Report unverified portions explicitly.
